N('dog_valves', 'Heart valves', 'organ', .02, ['dog_heart'], 'Four valves of thin flaps make the blood go one way: in, through, and out.',
  'The valves open and close with every heartbeat. The "lub-dub" sound is the valves closing.', 'The mitral valve (left) and tricuspid valve (right) lie between atrium and ventricle, and the aortic and pulmonary valves lie at the exits. Same set as in people. In older dogs the mitral valve may thicken and leak.', 'The model draws four rings at the approximate positions; they are placeholders for the valves, not valve shapes.', [['Number', '4']], cert='C2', refs=[A('19.1', '19-1-heart-anatomy')], human=[('mitral_valve', 'In people: the same four valves.'), ('aortic_valve', 'Compare the human aortic valve.')])
